  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Nothing is broken on our side. The lockouts came from your iPad's Mail app.\n\nYour password was reset yesterday at 4:05 PM, but the iPad still has the old password saved. Each time Mail retried it, the sign-in failed, and after five failures the account locked. The failures were all from that iPad between 9:48 and 9:52 AM.\n\nWhat I've done:\n- **Unlocked your account.** It's active again.\n- **Signed the iPad out** of your account, so it can't keep retrying the old password.\n\nWhat you need to do:\n1. On the iPad, open Mail and sign in with your **current** password. If you don't have it, I can send a reset link to your mobile or work email.\n2. If Mail asks you to re-add the account, do that. Your laptop and phone are working normally and don't need any changes.\n\nOnce you've signed in on the iPad, let me know and I'll confirm it's connected. If the lockouts continue after that, tell me and I'll look into it further."
  },
