  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I unlocked your account again, and it's active now. I also checked the sign-in log, and I can't find a failed sign-in from your phone.\n\nThe only failures in the log are the five from the iPad between 9:48 and 9:52. I revoked that iPad's session, and no new failures have been logged since. The lock you hit a few minutes ago may have been a delayed retry from the iPad, or the phone may have tried the old password from an app. I can't tell which from here.\n\nTo narrow it down:\n- **Which app were you using on the phone?** If it's Mail or another app with a saved password, that app needs your current password.\n- **Try signing in once more** on your laptop or phone. If the account locks again, tell me right away.\n- **Check the kids' iPad.** Your work email being on a home device is worth a look. If you find work accounts there that you don't recognize, or if the lockouts keep happening with no explanation, I can send this to Security to review."
  },
  {
   "role": "observation",
   "text": "[What you noticed]\n- You tried signing in again: it works.\nEverything IT has visibly done for you so far:\n- You tried signing in again a few minutes later: it says your account is locked again.\n- You tried signing in again: it works.\n[End of what you noticed]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok. I was signing in through the chat app on my phone when it locked. It's the same account, so I guess it's still using the password from somewhere.\n\nI just tried on my laptop and it worked fine. I'm not going to sign in on the iPad until I know what's going on with it. I'll check the Mail app on the phone too, I'm not sure what else has my work login saved. If it locks again I'll tell you right away."
  },
